{"c":[{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message, sent as error.says since H5); pin setGeneratorClock in offline measurements. Jev Choice confidence is the top-two margin (0.75 floor ~0.875 winner). Intent writer gpt-oss-120b: 8k tokens/min, space Ask evals 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads (since H5 sent as error.says), its detail holds the check's text. Offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold first forms are cut short.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice confidence is the margin between the top two option probabilities (a 0.75 floor needs ~0.875 on the winner). Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min; intents are ~2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1f86caa19701c852","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle() then routedSettled). Duplicate naps after a merge go at the next note. B27: score B17/B18 memory sets with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94b9c96f4bec8c25","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger (tests, evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on; routed producers hold offers, so await routing.idle() then routedSettled. I4: a merge of two branches that napped the same notes lists them twice until a note refolds.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233858Z-3b9ba7299adc0299","text":"I4: when two merged branches each napped the same notes, git keeps both naps and wake lists their lines twice (T2's 60b138f0/b105c8e9 vs H4's 7234fe4d); summem has no command to drop one, so fold before branching or accept the duplicate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7e9161a825c4d83","sum":"I4: after a merge with duplicate naps, the next summem note refolds and drops them; write a note and do its naps. B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last name 'none'; score with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T234020Z-7134731208a83f08","text":"I4 correction: the next summem note after such a merge re-plans the folds and drops the duplicate naps (one copy left per line, checked with recall); just write a note and do the naps it asks for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
